  "scope": "Stage 6b (D30, API D32): Luttinger-Tisza diagnostic at zero field.",
  "api": "spintoolkit.methods.luttinger_tisza(model, mesh=(48, 48)) -> LTReport (lambda_min, minima: LTWaveVector with fractional q*, fraction, supercell, multiplicity, strong_constraint, state, state_energy; near_minimal_fraction, extended_degeneracy); lt_matrix(model, q).",
  "method": "J(q)_ab = (1/2)[S_a S_b J exp(i q.(r_b - r_a)) + h.c.] over the bilinear terms (D13 full positions, unit vectors); lambda_min over a zone-centred mesh refined by Nelder-Mead; minima identified up to q -> -q and G; fractions with denominator <= 12 give the smallest supercell holding q*; the single-q strong constraint is fitted in the eigenspace (u_a . u_a = 0 and |u_a|^2 = 2 for generic q*, |Re u_a| = 1 when 2q* is a reciprocal vector, u_a = w_a exp(i q*.r_a)). Zeeman terms ignored; multi-q states and generalized LT not treated; the tool never selects the state.",
  "added": {
    "code-space/spintoolkit/methods/luttinger_tisza.py": "luttinger_tisza, lt_matrix, LTReport, LTWaveVector",
    "code-space/tests/test_methods/test_luttinger_tisza.py": "10 tests",
    "examples/luttinger_tisza_check.py": "this record"
  },
  "findings": [
    "J(q) reproduces the classical energy of random commensurate states on five models (triangular, J1-J2, honeycomb FM + DM, Kitaev, NBCP with J_PD) within 1.4e-16.",
